wsl-dns-forward for Debian
===========================

Installing this package does not change /etc/wsl.conf or /etc/resolv.conf,
because both are the administrator's to decide.  To finish the setup:

1. Add to /etc/wsl.conf:

     [network]
     generateResolvConf = false

     [boot]
     command = /usr/sbin/wsl-dns-forward -D -P /run/wsl-dns-forward.pid

2. Put 127.0.0.1 first in /etc/resolv.conf and keep the nameservers that are there now:

     sudo cp /etc/resolv.conf /etc/resolv.conf.pre-wsl-dns-forward
     { echo "nameserver 127.0.0.1"; grep '^nameserver' /etc/resolv.conf.pre-wsl-dns-forward | head -2; } \
         | sudo tee /etc/resolv.conf.new >/dev/null && sudo mv -f /etc/resolv.conf.new /etc/resolv.conf

3. Run "wsl --shutdown" from Windows and reopen WSL.

If libnss-mdns is installed, make the hosts line of /etc/nsswitch.conf
"hosts: files dns", or its mdns entry will stop .local lookups before they
reach DNS.

A systemd unit is installed but not enabled, for distributions with
systemd=true:  systemctl enable --now wsl-dns-forward

The full guide, with troubleshooting, is in README.md; the diagnostic
messages are explained in wsl-dns-forward(8).
